  "id": "conventionalism",
  "term": "conventionalism",
  "definition": "In this historical language context, conventionalism means reliance on shared social conventions to carry meaning, so less has to be marked explicitly in the form of words. It describes a more convention-dependent style, contrasted with forms that spell out each modification more directly.",
